# Git workflow & localhost preview

**One local checkout = one branch in the browser.** `localhost:4321` serves whatever branch is checked out in this repo folder. The user controls preview via Cursor’s **Checkout branch** on a chat — not by agents switching branches silently.

## Never checkout without permission

- Do **not** run `git checkout`, `git switch`, or create a branch that checks out locally unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. they clicked Checkout branch in that chat, or said “check out …”).
- Before any git operation, run `git branch --show-current` and mention which branch you’re on if it matters.

## Parallel work (other chats / features)

- Prefer **cloud agents** for side features so commits push to GitHub without changing the user’s local checkout.
- Local alternative: **git worktree** in a sibling folder (e.g. `../VCDwebsite-<branch>`) — never steal the main repo checkout for parallel edits.
- Do **not** start unrelated feature work on the user’s current preview branch without asking.

## Commits

- Only stage and commit files changed **in this chat session**. Leave other unstaged edits alone.
- One logical change set per branch/PR. Say which branch commits land on.

## PRs and main

- **Open PR** ≠ merge. Merge only when the user asks.
- After merge, preview `main` with: `git checkout main && git pull`, then reload the browser.
- Production deploys from `main` push (Cloudflare Pages).

## Dev session

Reuse the existing dev session (`bun run dev:session:status`) — do not start duplicate servers. See `dev-session.mdc`.
